  "info": {
    "description": "The local SQLite replica of what the sources hold, described as an API so that sdkgen can generate the access layer in every port.\n\nTHE PATHS ARE NOMINAL. Nothing here is served over HTTP. The generated SDK's transport is replaced by a `transport: 'base'` feature backed by SQLite, the same slot the SDKs' own offline test feature occupies. The paths exist because they are how sdkgen names an operation and derives an entity surface; they are never dialled.\n\nTHE REPLICA IS A CACHE AND NEVER A SOURCE OF TRUTH. Deleting the file loses nothing, every row records where it came from and when, and a write reaches here only after its source accepted it.",
    "title": "likeness replica",
    "version": "0.0.0"
  },
  "openapi": "3.0.3",
